  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Arabic ṯ corresponds to Hebrew š in this plant name. Kogan’s Proto-Semitic Lexicon (§4.4.2) also compares Mehri ṯəmēt and Jibbali ṯuhm, citing Johnstone’s Mehri Lexicon p. 417 and Jibbāli Lexicon p. 284. The biblical index files garlic under שול with the hem of a garment and several names. Its BDB key identifies the garlic token distinctly."
